{"assets":["/statement-assets/c2e8102832ac032f2c548c273335e2cca1dedaf79a7560c8c0fddc667d8f04c1.png","/statement-assets/af572790d886b5de9e6a69678560f5b9ffb802b8d91d49716b2f7199c5afce2c.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"633","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Startup Funding"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An e-commerce startup pitches to the investors to get funding. They have been functional for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" weeks now and also have a website!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each week they know the number of unique visitors during this week "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vi"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the revenue "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":". To evaluate the potential of the startup at some range of weeks from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" inclusive investors use the minimum among the maximum number of visitors multiplied by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"100"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the minimum revenue during this period, that is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c2e8102832ac032f2c548c273335e2cca1dedaf79a7560c8c0fddc667d8f04c1.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The truth is that investors have no idea how to efficiently evaluate the startup, so they are going to pick some "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" random distinct weeks "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li"},{"kind":"text","text":" and give them to managers of the startup. For each "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li"},{"kind":"text","text":" they should pick some "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ri ≥ li"},{"kind":"text","text":" and report maximum number of visitors and minimum revenue during this period."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then, investors will calculate the potential of the startup for each of these ranges and take minimum value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p(li, ri)"},{"kind":"text","text":" as the total evaluation grade of the startup. Assuming that managers of the startup always report the optimal values of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ri"},{"kind":"text","text":" for some particular "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li"},{"kind":"text","text":", i.e., the value such that the resulting grade of the startup is maximized, what is the expected resulting grade of the startup? "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ k ≤ n ≤ 1 000 000"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vi"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ vi ≤ 107"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of unique visitors during each week."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ci ≤ 107"},{"kind":"text","text":") —the revenue for each week."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single real value — the expected grade of the startup. Your answer will be considered correct if its absolute or relative error does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 6"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Namely: let's assume that your answer is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the answer of the jury is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":". The checker program will consider your answer correct, if "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/af572790d886b5de9e6a69678560f5b9ffb802b8d91d49716b2f7199c5afce2c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 2\n3 2 1\n300 200 300\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"133.3333333\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the first sample."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the investors ask for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" onwards, startup will choose "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ri = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", such that max number of visitors is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" and minimum revenue is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"300"},{"kind":"text","text":". Thus, potential in this case is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"min(3·100, 300) = 300"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the investors ask for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li = 2"},{"kind":"text","text":" onwards, startup will choose "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ri = 3"},{"kind":"text","text":", such that max number of visitors is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" and minimum revenue is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"200"},{"kind":"text","text":". Thus, potential in this case is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"min(2·100, 200) = 200"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the investors ask for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li = 3"},{"kind":"text","text":" onwards, startup will choose "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ri = 3"},{"kind":"text","text":", such that max number of visitors is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and minimum revenue is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"300"},{"kind":"text","text":". Thus, potential in this case is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"min(1·100, 300) = 100"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We have to choose a set of size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" equi-probably and take minimum of each. The possible sets here are : "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"{200, 300}"},{"kind":"text","text":","},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"{100, 300}"},{"kind":"text","text":","},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"{100, 200}"},{"kind":"text","text":", effectively the set of possible values as perceived by investors equi-probably: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"{200, 100, 100}"},{"kind":"text","text":". Thus, the expected value is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(100 + 200 + 100) / 3 = 133.(3)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"633E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/633/problem/E"}